# `pos` is asked for an int32 in front of the loop of scan(), and where the sum may have left the int32s it is asked again on the back edge: the failing side enters the closed copy of the loop for the next turn, with what
# comes round. No program with a text of ordinary length walks that way. Of the ways from a typed copy into its closed copy it was the one that FailGuesses did not take.
